# Local development: cp .env.example .env.local   (never commit .env files)
# Non-secret settings only.

# development | staging | production. Only production is indexable (src/app/robots.ts).
APP_ENV=development

# Server-side base URL of the API. On Railway: the api service's private domain (docs/railway.md).
# Local development: http://127.0.0.1:8000
API_INTERNAL_URL=https://api.staging.jackfixit.invalid

# The API's refresh token lifetime, mirrored for the admin panel's refresh cookie (#80): the same
# value as the api's REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS (2592000 by default). Required.
REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS=2592000

# Longest wait on the API for one server-side call, response body included, in milliseconds
# (#158). A silent API fails the call instead of hanging the page or the sign-out. Required.
API_TIMEOUT_MS=5000

# The KPI page (#84): the business time zone its presets ("Last 7 days") end today in, and the
# longest range it lets staff ask for. Optional, mirrors the api: set them only when the api's
# BUSINESS_TIME_ZONE or METRICS_MAX_RANGE_DAYS differ from their defaults (America/New_York,
# 366), which the page uses when these are unset.
# BUSINESS_TIME_ZONE=America/New_York
# METRICS_MAX_RANGE_DAYS=366

# Seconds between two reloads of the open operations queue in the panel (#81). Optional:
# half a minute when unset.
QUEUE_REFRESH_SECONDS=30

# The hours after which an open dispute's age turns amber, then red, in the panel's disputes (#83).
# Optional: 24 and 48 when unset (both are ignored unless red comes after amber).
# DISPUTE_AGE_WARN_HOURS=24
# DISPUTE_AGE_LATE_HOURS=48

# Public origin of this site (https, no path), read when the site is built. The landing (/, /es)
# and the showcase page (/app, /es/app) need it for their canonical, hreflang and Open Graph
# addresses, the sitemap, the robots.txt sitemap line and the landing's structured data, all of
# which must be absolute; without it the pages carry none of them and the sitemap is empty.
# Optional. On Railway: https://${{RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN}} or the custom domain.
# SITE_URL=https://staging.jackfixit.invalid

# The address of the landing page's Contact link (#85), as a mailto. Optional: without it (or
# with a value that is not an address) the footer has no Contact link. The page is built ahead
# and refreshed every hour, so a change shows within the hour.
# CONTACT_EMAIL=

# "true" once the web request flow (#86) ships: the landing then shows its "What's going on at
# home?" box and "Tell Jack What Happened". Anything else keeps "Get the app".
# REQUEST_FLOW_ENABLED=

# The showcase page's "tell me when the app is out" form (#409): "true" once POST /v1/interest
# exists. Read when /app and /es/app are built, so a change needs a deploy. While it is on, two
# secrets are required (Railway only, never here; at least 32 characters each, or the build
# fails): INTEREST_FORM_SECRET signs the form's token on this server, WEB_SERVICE_KEY identifies
# this web service to the API. CLIENT_IP_HEADER (the one edge header holding the visitor's
# address; its last value is used) is shared with the web request flow (#86).
# INTEREST_FORM_ENABLED=
# How old the form's token must be to send and may be at most, in seconds: 3 and 7200 when unset.
# INTEREST_FORM_MIN_SECONDS=3
# INTEREST_FORM_MAX_AGE_SECONDS=7200
# The web request flow (#86, /request and /es/request), read only while REQUEST_FLOW_ENABLED is
# "true". Two secrets are required then and live in Railway, never here: REQUEST_FORM_SECRET
# signs the form's token on this server, WEB_SERVICE_KEY identifies this web service to the API;
# each at least 32 characters, or the page fails rather than show a form it cannot send.
# The one request header the edge puts the visitor's address in (its last value is used), sent to
# the API with the key; unset, no address is forwarded. Check which header Railway's edge sets
# with a spoofed X-Forwarded-For on staging before turning the flow on.
# CLIENT_IP_HEADER=x-forwarded-for
# How old the form's token must be to send and may be at most, in seconds: 3 and 7200 when unset.
# REQUEST_FORM_MIN_SECONDS=3
# REQUEST_FORM_MAX_AGE_SECONDS=7200
# The calling code phone numbers are sent with (US numbers only, #138): +1 when unset.
# PHONE_COUNTRY_CODE=+1
# The app's store pages for the "sent" screen's invitation to make an account in the app. Set
# both once the app is in the stores; until then the screen links to /app.
# APP_STORE_URL=
# PLAY_STORE_URL=
